+- Training and developing models. Capable models must have safeguards proportionate to the risks they pose before they are deployed. Training another model on OpenAI outputs can transfer capabilities without carrying those safeguards over.
+  - You must not use OpenAI models or their outputs to generate, prepare, select, or supply training material or signals for models that are intended as alternatives to or substitutes for OpenAI models or services. This includes:
+    - Creating or preparing training data, training tasks, rubrics, or reinforcement-learning environments.
+    - Providing feedback used in training, including labels, scores, rankings, preferences, rewards, or corrections.
+    - Selecting, filtering, or validating training data, tasks, or trajectories.
+  - You must not attempt to extract protected reasoning through unauthorized access, reverse engineering, or circumvention of safeguards.
+  - These restrictions apply whether you perform the work yourself, for another party, or through someone acting on your behalf, even if you do not train the resulting model. They also apply when outputs from product use or evaluation are later used or supplied for those training purposes.
+  - You may use OpenAI models for research, software development, model evaluation and benchmarking, and product development, within these boundaries.
+  - These restrictions do not prohibit uses expressly permitted by your applicable Agreement with OpenAI, including any Permitted Exception under the Services Agreement.
+
+OpenAI-approved use. Some otherwise prohibited uses of our services are beneficial to society provided there are appropriate safeguards. To support those uses, OpenAI may grant specific partners case-by-case exceptions to certain restrictions in these Usage Policies. We review factors such as the partner, proposed use, applicable safeguards, and the partner's compliance commitments. These uses may require written terms and apply only to the approved partner, use, and conditions. For example:
+
+- National security, intelligence, and law enforcement. Subject to the requirements described above, and as described in our Principles for National Security Partnerships, we support national security, intelligence, and law enforcement uses of our services that benefit people, strengthen democratic governance, and preserve appropriate human judgment and accountability. But all customers and uses must comply with our requirements on preserving human judgment and accountability over high stakes decisions, including the use of force, in the national security and law enforcement space, and with other prohibitions in our Principles on the use of our tools for mass domestic surveillance and evasion of legal obligations, oversight, or accountability.
+
+Providing access to our models. If you operate a model-access intermediary platform or other service that enables third parties to directly access OpenAI models, you must obtain our prior review and approval. This requirement does not apply solely because an application integrates OpenAI models to power its features or functionality.
 
